@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Samsung modules callback hardening
+
+Base native source: `3a65e96f3694f19abd7feb1f905e4794f48d5aee`.
+Motivation: upstream `inforcqb/susfs4ksu-for-lkm` PR #200.
+
+The previous Samsung module always registered `m_show` by name. A duplicate
+name could select another callback, whose second argument was then read as a
+module list entry. Upstream removes the unvalidated fallback; this adaptation
+also preserves the entry-registration behavior which passed the Samsung phone
+tests. It does not restore the live `m->op == modules_op` gate that regressed
+root module hiding on S948B/BZIG.
+
+The loader resolves and validates `modules_op.show` using the existing
+core-symbol/body and CFI-stub checks. The by-name probe remains inert while the
+kernel registers it. Its actual resolved address must equal the verified
+callback entry, or follow just its BTI landing instruction; an adjustment past
+PAC or any other instruction is refused. A failed check unregisters the probe
+and leaves module-row filtering inactive with a warning. No unverified
+name-only filtering is enabled. Teardown closes callback admission before
+unregistering the probe.
+
+After admission, the module name is copied into a fixed-size local buffer
+through `copy_from_kernel_nofault`. Pointer underflow/overflow, unreadable data
+and names without a terminator are rejected before the name matcher runs.
+
+The full host deck passes 66 runner executions across 34 suites. New production
+extraction tests cover registration races, duplicate names, failure cleanup,
+CFI/BTI entry handling and the Samsung regression; three deliberately broken
+implementations are rejected. These results are not device validation.
+
+The existing symbol resolver, mount implementation, syscall wrappers, loader,
+root backends and SusFS ABI/version remain unchanged. A candidate APK must be
+phone-tested before this source is treated as a qualified replacement for the
+currently shipped module.
